{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add your app’s own state to every report, so the agent sees what the screenshot can’t show."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your app knows things ScreenClip can’t see: the signed-in account, what’s in the cart, which feature flags are on, the last request the backend answered. Register an attachment provider and its files travel with every report, next to the built-in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["#if DEBUG","ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"cart\") { context in","  let cart = await MainActor.run { CartStore.shared.snapshot }  \/\/ any Encodable","  return [try .json(cart, name: \"cart\", summary: \"the cart's \\(cart.items.count) items and promo codes\")]","}","#endif"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The agent reads each file’s name and summary in its prompt. It opens a file only when the screenshot and note aren’t enough, so write the summary for it: say what is inside."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attachment providers need ScreenClipKit 1.2.0 or later."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"When the provider runs","anchor":"When-the-provider-runs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach logs and diagnostics"}]},{"text":" enabled, the provider starts when the report sheet opens. It can read the app state while the tester annotates. Turning diagnostics on later starts a fresh provider run with the same report ID and capture time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", ScreenClip waits up to ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" more (5 seconds by default, at most 30) with ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Saving report…"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on screen. It then sends the report without whatever hasn’t arrived."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The provider runs off the main actor. Read main-actor state with ","type":"text"},{"code":"await MainActor.run { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and keep heavy work out of that closure.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Several files, async work, and context","type":"heading","anchor":"Several-files-async-work-and-context","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A provider returns any number of attachments. Return an empty array to add nothing this time."}]},{"code":["ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"account\", timeout: .seconds(10)) { context in","  let session = await MainActor.run { Session.current }","  guard let session else { return [] }","  let flags = try await FeatureFlags.shared.current()","  APILog.shared.mark(\"ScreenClip report \\(context.reportID)\")","  return [","    try .json(session.debugSummary, name: \"account\", summary: \"signed-in account, plan, and region\"),","    .text(flags.description, name: \"feature-flags\", summary: \"remote feature flags in effect\"),","    .text(await APILog.shared.recent(20), name: \"api-requests\", summary: \"last 20 backend requests and status codes\"),","  ]","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" carries the report’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reportID"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capturedAt"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenTitle"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenPath"},{"type":"text","text":". Log the report id next to your own records, such as a backend request id or an analytics session, to tie them to the report."}]},{"text":"Cancellation and failure","type":"heading","anchor":"Cancellation-and-failure","level":3},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provider is cancelled when the tester cancels the report, or turns off "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Attach logs and diagnostics","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Use cancellable APIs or check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.isCancelled"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the provider throws or misses its timeout, only its own files are left out. The report is still sent, and a line is logged under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenClipKit"},{"type":"text","text":" subsystem."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Registering and removing","anchor":"Registering-and-removing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each id holds one provider. Registering the same id again replaces it, so calling "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from an initializer or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"type":"text","text":" is safe. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" removes it. Providers run concurrently, and their files are listed in registration order."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Names and limits","anchor":"Names-and-limits"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" becomes a file name the Mac accepts. It is lowercased, anything other than letters, digits, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" becomes ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and it is cut to 32 characters, plus ","type":"text"},{"code":".txt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":".json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A name already in use, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"logs.txt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or another provider’s, gets ","type":"text"},{"code":"-2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"-3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and so on.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each attachment can be up to 1 MB ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes"},{"type":"text","text":"). Larger ones are left out."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A report takes up to 16 attachments (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumCount","isActive":true},{"text":"). Later ones are left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All files in a report share a 4 MB limit. When a report is over it, the largest files are dropped first."}]}]}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What not to attach","anchor":"What-not-to-attach"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t attach secrets. On the Mac, token-like strings are hidden in text files, but JSON files are stored as sent. Any attached file can be read by an agent working on the report.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Release builds "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does nothing, and the closure is never called. Keep the call inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if DEBUG"},{"type":"text","text":" anyway, so the code that gathers the data stays out of Release too."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/AttachingYourOwnFiles","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Attaching-your-own-data","title":"Attaching your own data"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenClipKit"}],"title":"Attaching your own files","role":"article"},"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/attachingyourownfiles"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"screenclip-icon.svg":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/screenclip-icon.svg","traits":["1x","light"]}],"identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg","alt":"The ScreenClip icon","type":"image"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)":{"title":"removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/removeattachmentprovider(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Stops adding the files from the provider registered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeAttachmentProvider","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collects your app’s own attachments for a report. It runs off the main actor; read main-actor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"state with ","type":"text"},{"code":"await MainActor.run { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Throwing leaves this provider’s files out of the report.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachmentprovider"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumCount":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumcount","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"maximumCount","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumCount","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumCount","abstract":[{"text":"The most attachments ScreenClip sends with one report, across all providers. Later ones are left out.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)":{"title":"setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/setattachmentprovider(_:timeout:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Adds your app’s own files to every report: state, records, anything an agent would want","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to see next to the screenshot.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13ScreenClipKit0aB18AttachmentProvidera"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumBytes":{"abstract":[{"text":"The largest attachment ScreenClip sends. Larger ones are left out of the report.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumbytes","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","title":"maximumBytes","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumBytes"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipReportContext":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a provider knows about the report it is attaching to."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipreportcontext","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenClipReportContext","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","title":"ScreenClipReportContext","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenClipReportContext","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/Diagnostics":{"title":"Diagnostics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional files ScreenClipKit attaches, and how the tester controls them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/diagnostics","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A file your app adds to a report, next to ScreenClip’s own logs and diagnostics."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","title":"ScreenClipAttachment","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenClipAttachment","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Report what you see in your own iOS app, straight into ScreenClip on your Mac, where a coding agent fixes it.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit","type":"topic","title":"ScreenClipKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","images":[{"identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg","type":"icon"}]}}}